**[Should-fix] Doc claims identical semantics to the SQL path, but label matching now trims whitespace**

The comment says the in-memory evaluation has "the semantics of EvidenceStatusCountsForFilters". The SQL path compares `lower(el.labels_name) = lower(?)` and `lower(el.labels_value) = lower(?)` with no trimming, while `LoadLatestEvidenceStreams` and `labelfilter.MatchLabels` both `TrimSpace` names and values. A label stored as `svc=" ec2"` matched nothing before and now matches `svc=ec2` (and `!=` flips accordingly). The equivalence integration test only uses trimmed values, so it cannot catch this, and a future change relying on the comment could reintroduce a divergence silently.

**Why:** A documented equivalence that is not quite true invites future changes that assume it.
**Fix:** State the one difference in the comment (names and values are trimmed as well as case-folded, as in lineage) and add a whitespace-padded label to TestComplianceProgressMatchesPerControlCounts asserting the new behaviour explicitly rather than comparing against the old SQL for that case.
